    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105587" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχαντήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>,
			ὁ, in Anatomy, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>trochanter,</i> i. e. either of two
			<i>processes</i> at the head of the thigh bone, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				15.8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.309
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				312
			</span></i>, Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				1.316s
			</span></i>q. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> part of
			the stern of a ship, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> an instrument of
			torture, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>4 Ma.</u>
				8.13
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τήρια</span>
			).</div>
